Teddy Riner has announced his candidacy for the 2027 French presidential elections, against a backdrop of political tension across France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ce5d6ca-dc73-11f1-b3f0-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26313423095961.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ce5d6ca-dc73-11f1-b3f0-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26313423095961.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31b0fd42-dcae-11f1-98ec-1707acb054a7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:35:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Ukraine, Russia and US to resume peace talks in Abu Dhabi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-live-ukraine-russia-and-us-to-resume-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi</link><description>
Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States are meeting in Abu Dhabi for their first trilateral talks in more than nine months, as Washington pushes for an end to the war and Kyiv faces pressure to make territorial concessions. European representatives will also attend, amid fears that US President Donald Trump could press Ukraine to accept a deal on Moscow's terms. Follow our live blog for the latest events.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9bd61a5c-dcba-11f1-ad47-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25048606702382.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9bd61a5c-dcba-11f1-ad47-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25048606702382.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1097d2e-dcba-11f1-a827-7bad94ce420d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:09:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9bd61a5c-dcba-11f1-ad47-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25048606702382.jpg">© WAM, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macrons file new defamation lawsuit against US podcaster over transgender rumours</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261110-macrons-file-new-defamation-lawsuit-against-us-podcaster-over-transgender-rumours</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron and his wife Brigitte filed a second lawsuit against US right-wing podcaster Candace Owens over false claims on her gender, accusing her of continuing to spread the allegations and profiting from them despite earlier legal action. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef3af00a-dcbf-11f1-b34e-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/cb700a478b2bb0246e753a3e44c0a699e13978e9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef3af00a-dcbf-11f1-b34e-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/cb700a478b2bb0246e753a3e44c0a699e13978e9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">efe09190-dcbf-11f1-9487-5f60e87d1ec6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:33:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef3af00a-dcbf-11f1-b34e-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/cb700a478b2bb0246e753a3e44c0a699e13978e9.jpg">© Abdul Saboor, POOL/AFP/File</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>California voters reject proposed one-time tax on billionaires' wealth</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-california-voters-reject-proposed-one-time-tax-on-billionaires-wealth</link><description>
California voters have rejected a proposed 5% tax on the net worth of billionaires, handing a victory to tech leaders who poured hundreds of millions of dollars into defeating the measure. The defeat of Proposition 40 also marks a setback for progressives seeking to tax the wealth of the ultra-rich.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bfc22d4-d82f-11f1-844d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/billionaire-calif-taxe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bfc22d4-d82f-11f1-844d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/billionaire-calif-taxe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9abd1fc6-dcb5-11f1-86a2-c33df443f3e0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:19:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bfc22d4-d82f-11f1-844d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/billionaire-calif-taxe.jpg">© Jeff Chiu, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Amnesty urges El Salvador to disclose terms of Haiti troop deployment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261110-amnesty-urges-el-salvador-to-disclose-terms-of-haiti-troop-deployment</link><description>
Amnesty International has called on El Salvador and Haiti to make public the agreement governing the deployment of around 2,000 Salvadoran troops to the gang-plagued Caribbean nation, warning of risks to human rights and accountability.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a2090b6-dcad-11f1-9ef2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26303760183098.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a2090b6-dcad-11f1-9ef2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26303760183098.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7c08faa-dcad-11f1-87eb-470690c58bc4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:24:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a2090b6-dcad-11f1-9ef2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26303760183098.jpg">© Odelyn Joseph, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nvidia shares slide as board probes CEO over affair with alleged Chinese spy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-nvidia-shares-slide-as-board-probes-ceo-over-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy</link><description>
Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang is facing scrutiny after reports he was targeted in a suspected Chinese intelligence operation involving a businesswoman with whom he was having an affair. The controversy has rattled investors, sending Nvidia shares tumbling.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5d81122-dc9b-11f1-b602-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261110-000700-000840-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5d81122-dc9b-11f1-b602-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261110-000700-000840-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bae13162-dc9b-11f1-b7b9-5fa467cf057b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:22:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Defense Secretary Hegseth faces expected impeachment vote this week</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-hegseth-faces-expected-impeachment-vote-this-week</link><description>
A Republican lawmaker moved Monday to impeach US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth over the war in Iran, setting up a potentially explosive vote in Congress days after President Donald Trump's party suffered a crushing midterm defeat. Kentucky congressman Thomas Massie introduced eight articles of impeachment accusing Hegseth of illegally waging war without congressional authorization and abusing his powers as Pentagon chief. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20a94370-dc8f-11f1-a9ca-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-233324-233828-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20a94370-dc8f-11f1-a9ca-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-233324-233828-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">259522b4-dc8f-11f1-b840-153c8e20bd71</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:51:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France blames Iran for cyberattack on supermarket fridges</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-france-blames-iran-for-cyberattack-on-supermarket-fridges</link><description>
French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being behind a recent cyberattack on French supermarket fridges, saying there would be consequences for the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37a1d2ea-dc8a-11f1-b381-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-230143-230334-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37a1d2ea-dc8a-11f1-b381-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-230143-230334-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3c6fe140-dc8a-11f1-9bdb-cd54f6160d1a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:33:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Nvidia: honeypot may have been aimed at 'lobbying Jensen Huang to lobby the US government'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261109-nvidia-honeypot-may-have-been-aimed-at-lobbying-jensen-huang-to-lobby-the-us-government</link><description>
Nvidia ⁠and ​Chief ​Executive Jensen Huang were ​sued ‌on ⁠Monday ‌in ⁠a proposed class ​action accusing ‌them of ‌defrauding ​shareholders by concealing Huang's ties ​with ​a ​suspected ​Chinese spy. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Steve Tsang, Director of the SOAS China Institute, says that the affair "can also be about effectively lobbying Jensen Huang to lobby the US government, because he is a very powerful figure, particularly during the Trump administration, and he, for whatever reason, has been taking a position that is beneficial to Chinese development and advancement of its AI capacity".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd78160c-dc88-11f1-88e7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-223117-224317-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd78160c-dc88-11f1-88e7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-223117-224317-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a746292-dc8b-11f1-83d5-a1da707764f7</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:17:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nvidia: honeypot may have been aimed at 'lobbying Jensen Huang to lobby the US government'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nvidia-honeypot-may-have-been-aimed-at-lobbying-jensen-huang-to-lobby-the-us-government</link><description>
Nvidia ⁠and ​Chief ​Executive Jensen Huang were ​sued ‌on ⁠Monday ‌in ⁠a proposed class ​action accusing ‌them of ‌defrauding ​shareholders by concealing Huang's ties ​with ​a ​suspected ​Chinese spy. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Steve Tsang, Director of the SOAS China Institute, says that the affair "can also be about effectively lobbying Jensen Huang to lobby the US government, because he is a very powerful figure, particularly during the Trump administration, and he, for whatever reason, has been taking a position that is beneficial to Chinese development and advancement of its AI capacity".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd78160c-dc88-11f1-88e7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-223117-224317-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd78160c-dc88-11f1-88e7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-223117-224317-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">029694c4-dc89-11f1-9bae-e94aadb961b2</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:14:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK writer M. John Harrison wins Booker Prize for AI-tinged apocalyptic novel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-uk-writer-m-john-harrison-wins-booker-prize-for-ai-tinged-apocalyptic-novel</link><description>
UK author M. John Harrison won the Booker Prize on Monday for his enigmatic novel "The End of Everything", which echoes concerns about artificial intelligence in a darkly satirical depiction of post-apocalyptic Britain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a8ae5c2-dc8a-11f1-aa1e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/b494e954a69a687575dd83c9c41ab832139bc0fd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a8ae5c2-dc8a-11f1-aa1e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/b494e954a69a687575dd83c9c41ab832139bc0fd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4bbbc5a6-dc8a-11f1-8036-c3ccd3b6a869</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:09:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a8ae5c2-dc8a-11f1-aa1e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/b494e954a69a687575dd83c9c41ab832139bc0fd.jpg">© Justin Tallis, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>South Africa’s ANC suffers a historic setback in local elections as coalition talks begin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261109-south-africa-s-anc-suffers-a-historic-setback-in-local-elections-as-coalition-talks-begin</link><description>
South Africa’s ruling ANC suffers its worst-ever local election results, securing just 30% of the vote, as coalition talks loom. Meanwhile, former Ugandan military intelligence officer Herbert Matanda Mabonga accuses the army of secretly detaining and torturing opponents, following the release of videos that sparked national outrage. Finally, in Senegal, more than 200,000 free tickets are giving young people the chance to experience the games live on home soil, in a bid to inspire a new generation of athletes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/346c3b5e-dc87-11f1-b0e6-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-aa965032.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/346c3b5e-dc87-11f1-b0e6-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-aa965032.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1957d07a-dc88-11f1-b5dd-f70ded79d94a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 21:54:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clémence WALLER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What to expect as Russia, Ukraine and the US hold trilateral talks in Abu Dhabi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-what-to-expect-as-russia-ukraine-and-us-hold-trilateral-talks-in-abu-dhabi</link><description>
Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States are set to meet in the capital of the United Arab Emirates (UAE) on Tuesday for a new round of talks aimed at ending nearly five years of full-scale war triggered by Moscow's invasion of its neighbour. Security guarantees for the warring sides are set to top the agenda, with US officials insisting that a broader security architecture for Europe must be part of any peace deal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e77aaca-dc82-11f1-9693-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T090059Z-1254041086-RC26DNA29012-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-RUSSIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e77aaca-dc82-11f1-9693-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T090059Z-1254041086-RC26DNA29012-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-RUSSIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82ede6be-dc6f-11f1-b66f-c9c2e19e7715</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 21:46:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e77aaca-dc82-11f1-9693-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T090059Z-1254041086-RC26DNA29012-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-USA-RUSSIA.jpg">© Gavriil Grigorov, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French Judo superstar Teddy Riner says will run for president</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-judo-superstar-teddy-riner-says-will-run-for-president</link><description>
France's multiple Olympic judo champion Teddy Riner announced on Monday he would run in next year's presidential election, after expressing concern about the "rise of the far right". "My name is Teddy Riner and today, I am telling you face to face: I am a candidate in the 2027 presidential election," the 37-year-old said in a surprise announcement on social media. Riner, one of the greatest judokas in history, said in the two-minute-37-second video that he feared France could soon become deeply divided, appearing to cast himself as a candidate for voters unwilling to choose between two political extremes -- the far right and the hard left. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Yves Sintomer, Professor of Political Science at Université Paris VIII.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f62a8bcc-dc7f-11f1-ad8f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-213456-214006-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f62a8bcc-dc7f-11f1-ad8f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-213456-214006-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb2c97c8-dc7f-11f1-a762-f3f1ad594750</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 21:14:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump says he was ‘kidding’ about Dana White press secretary job, amid online mix-up claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261109-trump-says-he-was-kidding-about-dana-white-press-secretary-job-amid-online-mix-up-claims</link><description>
Donald Trump says he was "only kidding" when he announced he had offered his friend and UFC boss Dana White the job of White House press secretary. The president shared an AI-generated video of White behind the briefing room podium and UFC fighters attacking journalists. But the announcement also sparked online speculation that Trump may have confused the UFC executive with a former Pentagon spokesperson, also called Dana White. There's no evidence of a mix-up, as Vedika Bahl explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46f18494-dc7f-11f1-80b4-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/dana-white.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46f18494-dc7f-11f1-80b4-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/dana-white.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5928d950-dc7f-11f1-8620-f5cafcaad1e3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:51:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nvidia's Huang scandal rattles AI industry built around him</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nvidia-s-huang-scandal-rattles-ai-industry-built-around-him</link><description>
Nvidia chief Jensen Huang sits at the center of the artificial intelligence boom, and the spy scandal that erupted over the weekend threatens to shake the company at a time when confidence in the AI investment frenzy is already fragile. Taiwan-born Huang is regarded as the godfather of the AI economy, the executive every player in the industry must turn to because the technology depends on the graphics processing units (GPUs) that his company designs. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet reports from Los Angeles.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0c0757c-dc77-11f1-97b1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-203701-204148-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b0c0757c-dc77-11f1-97b1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-203701-204148-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b5a790ac-dc77-11f1-aa46-e978521f0d42</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:09:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paris prosecutor opens probe into IRGC cyber unit Shahid Kaveh over fridge cyberattacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/paris-prosecutor-opens-probe-into-irgc-cyber-unit-shahid-kaveh-over-fridge-cyberattacks</link><description>
The Paris prosecutor said she had opened an investigation into Shahid Kaveh, a shadowy cyber unit of the IRGC, the Islamic republic's ideological army, over the 'unprecedented' cyberattacks targeting French supermarkets' fridges in October. Little is known about the Shahid Kaveh unit, although analysts have long observed that the IRGC, which has a vast network of operations, had actively branched out into cyber warfare in recent years. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93dd0826-dc77-11f1-8ea8-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-203104-203701-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93dd0826-dc77-11f1-8ea8-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-203104-203701-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">98bdc0ec-dc77-11f1-813e-1967698c37ee</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:06:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault</link><description>
British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape, as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him. Brand, 51, showed no emotion as judge Joel Bennathan said he had acted with "staggering arrogance" and shown "contempt" for his victims, who had suffered significant and lasting harm. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6830bca-dc76-11f1-ad17-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-201213-201409-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6830bca-dc76-11f1-ad17-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-201213-201409-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc339a6c-dc76-11f1-a4b3-a141c2237e68</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:03:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Will Eisenkot succeed in 'minefield of Israeli politics' where 'so many other generals' have failed?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261109-will-eisenkot-succeed-in-minefield-of-israeli-politics-where-so-many-other-generals-have-failed</link><description>
François Picard welcomes Dahlia Scheindlin, Israeli author, political analyst, strategic consultant and pollster, to examine a question that reaches far beyond the immediate struggle for power: Can Israel move beyond Netanyahu amid coalition deadlock, growing disillusionment in Washington and the persistent limits of political inclusion? As Gadi Eisenkot embarks on a 45-day race to form a government, following Israeli President Isaac Herzog's decision to entrust him with the task of assembling an elusive parliamentary majority, Scheindlin offers a timely reminder: “It's always too early to eulogize Netanyahu politically.” seemingly insurmountable political crises.
